+	depends on PCI && DMA_ENGINE
+	help
+	  Exposes the DDR3 memory of the Baikal southbridge (PCI 00:14.6) as
+	  /dev/baikal_spm0, moved by the baikal-dmac DMA engine, so it can be
+	  used as a fast swap device:
+
+	    mkswap /dev/baikal_spm0 && swapon -p 50 /dev/baikal_spm0
+
+	  Only the first 188 MiB of the memory answer on the console this was
+	  measured on, so the device is at most that size. Without a DMA channel
+	  it falls back to CPU copies, which are about 20 times slower.
